course: dictionary
lesson: 9656
title: Submissive: giving in without a fight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Submissive means willing to do what others want, without arguing or standing up for yourself. Look at the clues in the sentence: «When Toad's quiet and submissive and playing at being the hero of a Sunday-school prize, then he's at his artfullest.» Toad is quiet and does what others want, so he seems meek.
explain: But the Badger is warning everyone that Toad is only playing a part. The words "playing at being" tell you the submissive look is a show, not the truth. The word "then" tells you that when Toad seems most meek, he is most sly. Context gives you the meaning and the author's feeling.
explain: Animals show submissive behaviour too. A puppy lies down and a wolf tucks its tail to show a stronger animal that it will not fight. This is body language that says "I am not a threat." Being respectful is different from being submissive: you can respect people and still say no.
fact: Submissive means willing to obey others and not argue or stand up for yourself.
fact: «Submissive» is an adjective. The adverb is submissively and the noun is submission.
fact: For animals, submissive means showing by body language that they will not fight, like a dog rolling on its back.
fact: If anyone pressures you to do something wrong or unsafe, you can say no and tell a trusted adult.
fact: You can be polite and respectful without being submissive.
exercise: In «When Toad's quiet and submissive...», what does submissive mean? | Very tall | Loud and bold | *Willing to do what others want, without standing up for yourself | Hungry for food
exercise: A puppy lies on its back when a bigger dog comes near. What is it showing? | *It will not fight | It is asleep and cannot see | It wants to start a fight | It is hungry
exercise: Which word is the noun form of submissive? | *submission | subject | submarine | submissively
test: The Badger says Toad is only pretending to be submissive. What does pretending suggest? | Toad is angry and loud | *Toad is acting, and may be sly | Toad is asleep | Toad is truly meek and kind
test: A friend pressures you to do something unsafe. What is the best response? | *Say no and tell a trusted adult | Do it to keep your friend happy | Hide and say nothing | Agree quietly because you are submissive
exam: Which sentence uses submissively correctly? | He ran submissively across the playground | *She nodded submissively and let the others choose | The submissively dog was loud | She shouted submissively at the teacher
